@startuml Tapping Trigger System
!theme plain
title Tapping System — 7 Combinable Triggers\nEnable any subset; arm with F2; highest-priority trigger wins

[*] --> IDLE

state "IDLE\n(tapping_armed = false)" as IDLE {
  IDLE : Triggers configured but inactive
  IDLE : Motor runs normally (DRL state)
}

state "ARMED\n(tapping_armed = true)" as ARMED {
  state "Monitoring" as MON
  state "Triggered" as TRIG
  state "Reversing" as REV
  state "Completing" as COMP

  MON --> TRIG : Any enabled trigger fires
  TRIG --> REV : CMD_MOTOR_TAP_REVERSE\n(polls GF bit 2 for direction change)
  REV --> COMP : Completion action\n(Stop / RevOut / RevTime)
  COMP --> MON : Cycle complete
}

IDLE --> ARMED : F2 press\n(at least 1 trigger enabled)
ARMED --> IDLE : F2 press (disarm)\nor motor stopped

note right of ARMED
  **7 Triggers (combinable)**

  | Code | Trigger | Priority |
  | P | Pedal | 1 (highest) |
  | Q | Quill | 2 |
  | D | Depth | 3 |
  | I | Load Inc | 4 |
  | S | Load Slip | 4 |
  | C | Clutch | 4 |
  | K | Peck | 5 (lowest) |

  Enable in Menu > Tapping
  Display: "DIQ" = Depth+Inc+Quill active
end note

note bottom
  **Tapping Task (20Hz, Priority 3)**

  Reads from g_state:
  • current_depth, motor_running
  • motor_load (KR), motor_forward
  • tapping_armed, pedal_pressed

  Checks settings_get():
  • Individual trigger enables
  • Per-trigger thresholds/timing

  Commands Motor via queue:
  • CMD_MOTOR_TAP_FORWARD
  • CMD_MOTOR_TAP_REVERSE
  • CMD_MOTOR_STOP

  Direction change uses GF bit 2 polling
  (waits for MCB commutation switch complete)
end note

@enduml
